// Game: Postretro
// Format: Standard
// Level seam pair, map A. Map B is seam-pair-b.map.
// Compile: cargo run -p postretro-level-compiler -- content/dev/maps/seam-pair-a.map -o content/dev/maps/seam-pair-a.prl
// TrenchBroom units, 1 unit = 0.0254 m, floor top at z 0.
// Room interior x 0 to 512, y 0 to 384, ceiling z 256. A doorway in the east wall at y 160 to 224 opens
// onto a hallway, interior x 576 to 832, y 160 to 224, ceiling z 128, capped at its east end.
// Seam pair_door covers the hallway at x 640 to 768, targets catalog id seam-pair-b, and carries tag airlock.
// The data script disarms the seam a player arrives by; the airlock_button trigger in the room arms it again.
// Its landmark pair_landmark stands on the hallway floor at 704 192 0, yaw 0.
// Map B holds the same hallway about a landmark at yaw 90, so walking east here walks north there.
// Every brush is an axis-aligned box. Keep comments free of braces and quotes.
// entity 0
